1
00:02:27,530 --> 00:02:31,000
[ Boy ] What's your name again ? Chrissie.

2
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,030
Where we goin' ? Swimming.

3
00:02:35,710 --> 00:02:37,200
Slow up.

4
00:02:38,110 --> 00:02:40,170
Slow down.

5
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:42,770
I'm not drunk. Slow down.

6
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:48,890
Wait! I'm coming. I'm coming.

7
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:53,520
I'm definitely coming. [ Giggling ]

8
00:02:53,630 --> 00:02:55,120
Whoa ! Hold on.

9
00:03:04,610 --> 00:03:06,000
I can swim.

10
00:03:06,910 --> 00:03:09,840
I just can't walk or undress myself. [ Chuckling ]

11
00:03:30,060 --> 00:03:31,620
Come on in the water !

12
00:03:31,730 --> 00:03:33,500
Take it easy. Take it easy.

13
00:04:20,380 --> 00:04:21,540
Help me !

14
00:04:21,650 --> 00:04:24,550
[ Whispering ] I'm coming. I'm coming.

15
00:04:32,990 --> 00:04:35,890
Oh, my God !

16
00:04:39,630 --> 00:04:41,100
Oh, God !

17
00:04:42,670 --> 00:04:44,730
Oh, God, no ! God, no !

18
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:46,740
Please help !

19
00:05:05,030 --> 00:05:07,550
[ Radio ] Local fishing reported good...

20
00:05:07,660 --> 00:05:09,630
and many boat rental yards opening early...

21
00:05:09,730 --> 00:05:11,820
to prepare for the annual seasonal rush.

22
00:05:11,930 --> 00:05:13,830
This is W-I-S-S-- [ Groaning ]

23
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:20,840
[ Man ] How come the sun didn't use to shine in here ?

24
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:25,940
We bought the house in the fall...

25
00:05:26,050 --> 00:05:27,450
and this is summer.

26
00:05:31,590 --> 00:05:34,320
Somebody feed the dogs, huh ?

27
00:05:34,450 --> 00:05:35,820
Right.

28
00:05:39,530 --> 00:05:40,990
Do you see the kids ?

29
00:05:41,630 --> 00:05:44,100
[ Radio ] ... forecast calls for clear skies and fair weather...

30
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:46,130
at least through the regatta weekend.

31
00:05:46,230 --> 00:05:49,200
They must be in the backyard.

32
00:05:49,300 --> 00:05:51,670
In Amity you say ''yahd.''

33
00:05:51,770 --> 00:05:58,000
They're in the ''yahd,'' Not too ''farh'' from the ''carh.''

34
00:05:58,110 --> 00:06:02,150
How's that ? Like you're from New York.

35
00:06:04,020 --> 00:06:07,250
Mom, I got cut. I got hit by a vampire.

36
00:06:07,390 --> 00:06:09,860
You guys were playin' on those swings. [ Phone Ringing ]

37
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:12,660
Those swings are dangerous. Stay off there. Yuk.

38
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:18,030
[ Dial Tone ] I think you're gonna live. Hello. It's not the biggest thing I've ever seen.

39
00:06:18,170 --> 00:06:20,460
Yeah. Can I go swimmin' ?

40
00:06:20,570 --> 00:06:22,470
Yeah, but let me clean this first.

41
00:06:22,570 --> 00:06:25,200
What do they usually do, wash up or float or what ?

42
00:06:25,410 --> 00:06:27,840
Make sure you don't go past the jetty.

43
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:31,550
Oh, no, no, no. Keep 'em there. I'll be out...

44
00:06:31,550 --> 00:06:37,470
in about fifteen, twenty minutes, all right ?

45
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:39,480
Okay. Get a Band-Aid.

46
00:06:39,590 --> 00:06:42,760
[ Man ] Gotta go... missing person.

47
00:06:42,760 --> 00:06:44,920
Season hasn't started. Nobody's even here yet.

48
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:51,530
Listen, Chief,

49
00:06:51,530 --> 00:06:54,970
be careful, will ya ? In this town ? Hey. Bye, Dad.

50
00:06:54,970 --> 00:06:57,630
Wait. Let me get on.

51
00:06:57,740 --> 00:06:59,760
I want my cup back ! You'll get it.

52
00:07:01,580 --> 00:07:03,910
Wave good-bye. Bye !

53
00:07:23,730 --> 00:07:26,460
For folks at the beaches, we've got some safety tips for you.

54
00:07:26,630 --> 00:07:29,930
The safety council says --

55
00:07:33,670 --> 00:07:36,010
And nobody saw her go into the water ?

56
00:07:36,110 --> 00:07:40,740
Somebody could've. I was sort of passed out.

57
00:07:40,850 --> 00:07:43,040
You mean, she ran out on you ? No, sir.

58
00:07:45,750 --> 00:07:47,850
She must've drowned.

59
00:07:47,990 --> 00:07:50,460
Look, I reported it to you, didn't I ?

60
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:53,390
You live here ? No, Hartford.

61
00:07:53,490 --> 00:07:55,890
I go to Trinity. My folks live in Greenwich.

62
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,790
Your folks were born here ? Yeah, I'm an islander.

63
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:00,830
They moved off when my dad retired.

64
00:08:00,930 --> 00:08:03,130
You an islander ? No, New York City.

65
00:08:03,270 --> 00:08:05,200
You here for the summer ?

66
00:08:05,310 --> 00:08:06,600
C'mon.

67
00:08:19,450 --> 00:08:20,780
Hold it.

68
00:08:32,100 --> 00:08:36,560
[ Chief Brody ] Oh, Jesus.

69
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:02,030
Well, you're up awful early !

70
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:04,130
Is the chief in there ?

71
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:07,790
Well, Chief, what have you got on ?

72
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:09,870
Polly, if this filing system is going to work,

73
00:09:09,970 --> 00:09:11,870
keep outdated stuff off my desk;

74
00:09:11,970 --> 00:09:14,040
just the pending. Yes, Chief.

75
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:16,530
We've got a bunch of calls about that karate school.

76
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:19,580
It seems the nine year olds from the school... [ Buzzing ]

77
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:21,770
are ''karating'' the picket fences.

78
00:09:23,350 --> 00:09:26,550
Chief Brody's office. The medical inspector.

79
00:09:36,760 --> 00:09:41,870
The fire chief wants you to go over the 4th of July --

80
00:09:41,970 --> 00:09:43,990
I want a list of all the water activities...

81
00:09:44,100 --> 00:09:46,330
that the city fathers are planning for today. Right away ?

82
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:50,100
Hendricks, where do we keep the ''beach closed'' signs ? Chief?

83
00:09:50,210 --> 00:09:51,800
We never had any. No ?

84
00:09:51,910 --> 00:09:54,810
There's a dead truck smack in front of my store.

85
00:09:55,780 --> 00:09:58,010
[ Brody ] Just have him fill out the form.

86
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:59,680
Just fill it out.

87
00:10:21,210 --> 00:10:24,640
Look what the kids did to my fence. Eight or nine year olds. Hey, glasses, huh ?

88
00:10:24,640 --> 00:10:28,710
Yeah, glasses. Can I call you this afternoon ?

89
00:10:28,820 --> 00:10:30,250
I'll call you in the afternoon, I promise.

90
00:10:30,350 --> 00:10:34,290
[ Whistle ]

91
00:10:35,620 --> 00:10:38,220
This stuff isn't gonna help me in August.

92
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:41,090
The summer ginks come down here in June.

93
00:10:41,190 --> 00:10:43,820
You haven't got one thing on here I ordered.

94
00:10:43,930 --> 00:10:48,160
Not a beach umbrella, sun lounger, beach balls --

95
00:10:48,270 --> 00:10:51,140
If I can't get service --

96
00:10:55,110 --> 00:10:56,680
Chief !

97
00:10:56,680 --> 00:11:01,110
Chief, Polly sent me to find you... to tell you there's a bunch of boy scouts in Avril Bay...

98
00:11:01,110 --> 00:11:04,280
doin' their mile swim for their merit badges.

99
00:11:04,280 --> 00:11:06,510
I couldn't call them in. There's no phones out there.

100
00:11:06,620 --> 00:11:08,610
Okay, c'mon, get out.

101
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:11,620
Take this stuff to the office and get to work on those signs. All right.

102
00:11:11,730 --> 00:11:15,350
''Beaches closed, no swimming by order of the Amity P.D.''

103
00:11:15,460 --> 00:11:17,830
Let Polly do the printing. What's the matter with my printing ?

104
00:11:17,930 --> 00:11:19,900
Let Polly do the printing.

105
00:11:20,130 --> 00:11:21,600
Hey, Chief? Chief Brody !

106
00:11:25,270 --> 00:11:29,630
What have you got there ? We had a shark attack at South Beach this morning, Mayor.

107
00:11:29,740 --> 00:11:31,710
Fatal ! I've got to batten down the beach.

108
00:11:31,810 --> 00:11:33,840
Okay, Albert, Come on, you kook.

109
00:11:33,950 --> 00:11:35,810
Keep your arms up.

110
00:11:35,950 --> 00:11:38,210
Don't fight it. Let it carry you.

111
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:43,890
Charlie, take me out to those kids, will ya ?

112
00:12:05,480 --> 00:12:06,710
Martin ?

113
00:12:08,080 --> 00:12:11,380
You gonna shut down the beaches on your own authority ?

114
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:13,380
What other authority do I need ?

115
00:12:13,490 --> 00:12:16,050
Technically you need a civic ordinance or resolution.

116
00:12:16,190 --> 00:12:17,950
That's just going by the book.

117
00:12:18,090 --> 00:12:22,260
We're anxious that you're rushing into something serious.

118
00:12:22,360 --> 00:12:24,090
It's your first summer, you know ?

119
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:26,100
What does that mean ?

120
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:30,600
I'm only trying to say that Amity is a summer town.

121
00:12:30,700 --> 00:12:32,830
We need summer dollars.

122
00:12:32,940 --> 00:12:35,600
If the people can't swim here, they'll be glad to swim...

123
00:12:35,710 --> 00:12:38,840
at the beaches of Cape Cod, the Hamptons, Long Island.

124
00:12:38,950 --> 00:12:40,910
That doesn't mean we serve them a smorgasbord.

125
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:43,350
We never had that kind of trouble in these waters.

126
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:46,490
What else could have done that to that girl ? Boat propeller ?

127
00:12:46,590 --> 00:12:50,090
I think possibly, yes, a boating accident.

128
00:12:50,090 --> 00:12:52,760
That's not what you told me over the phone. I was wrong.

129
00:12:52,760 --> 00:12:56,130
We'll have to amend our reports.

130
00:12:56,130 --> 00:12:58,120
You'll stand by that ? I'll stand by that.

131
00:12:58,970 --> 00:13:02,500
Oh -- Martin... a summer girl

132
00:13:02,600 --> 00:13:04,400
goes swimming, swims out a little far.

133
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:08,000
She tires, a fishing boat comes along -- It's happened before.

134
00:13:08,110 --> 00:13:11,130
I don't think you appreciate the gut reaction people have to these things.

135
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:14,370
I appreciate it. I'm just reacting to what I was told.

136
00:13:14,450 --> 00:13:17,610
Martin, it's all psychological.

137
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:19,780
You yell ''barracuda'' ...

138
00:13:19,890 --> 00:13:21,880
and everybody says, ''Huh ? What ?''

139
00:13:23,390 --> 00:13:24,820
You yell ''shark,''

140
00:13:26,390 --> 00:13:29,090
we've got a panic on our hands on the 4th of July.

141
00:13:30,300 --> 00:13:33,530
Okay, you can take us back now.

142
00:13:45,580 --> 00:13:49,120
I'm gonna get my raft and go back out in the water.

143
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:50,670
Let me see your fingers.

144
00:13:52,090 --> 00:13:54,180
Alex Kintner, they're beginning to prune.

145
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:56,350
Just a little longer ?

146
00:13:56,490 --> 00:13:58,680
Just ten more minutes. Thanks.

147
00:14:03,830 --> 00:14:05,890
[ Woman ] All I want to know--

148
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:11,070
I want to know one, simple thing. When do I get to become an islander ?

149
00:14:11,170 --> 00:14:12,870
Ellen, never !

150
00:14:12,970 --> 00:14:15,500
You're not born here, you're not an islander.

151
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:21,770
Hey, Marty, I know you got a lot of problems downtown,

152
00:15:21,870 --> 00:15:24,500
but I got problems at the house I wish you could take care of.

153
00:15:24,580 --> 00:15:27,010
I've got cats parking in front of the house --

154
00:15:27,110 --> 00:15:28,580
[ Screaming ]

155
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:32,280
And that garbage truck next to the office has got to be moved.

156
00:15:32,390 --> 00:15:34,910
I need a red zone. It's a simple thing you could take care of.

157
00:15:35,050 --> 00:15:40,380
Honey, would you come here a minute, please ? Excuse me.

158
00:15:42,800 --> 00:15:44,390
Are you okay ?

159
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:45,990
Yeah, I'm fine.

160
00:15:46,100 --> 00:15:50,000
If the kids goin' in the water is worrying you --

161
00:15:50,100 --> 00:15:52,230
No, no. They can play out here on the beach.

162
00:15:52,340 --> 00:15:54,100
It's all right. Let them go.

163
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:05,280
It's cold.

164
00:16:05,390 --> 00:16:08,950
We know all about you, Chief.

165
00:16:09,090 --> 00:16:11,150
You don't go in the water at all, do you ?

166
00:16:11,290 --> 00:16:13,260
That's some bad hat, Harry.

167
00:16:19,430 --> 00:16:21,920
Chief Brody, you are uptight.

168
00:16:22,040 --> 00:16:23,970
C'mon...

169
00:16:25,140 --> 00:16:27,200
that's it.

170
00:16:27,340 --> 00:16:31,000
C'mon. [ Yelling And Laughing ]

171
00:16:33,980 --> 00:16:37,180
# Oh, do you know the muffin man #

172
00:16:37,280 --> 00:16:40,510
# The muffin man The muffin man # Pippet !

173
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:42,950
Pippet !

174
00:16:43,860 --> 00:16:45,320
Pippet ! C'mon, Pippet !

175
00:16:45,490 --> 00:16:49,020
Pippet!

176
00:17:10,650 --> 00:17:12,580
Did you see that ? Yeah.

177
00:17:21,230 --> 00:17:22,690
[ Yelling ]

178
00:17:27,630 --> 00:17:29,760
Get everybody out ! Get out !

179
00:17:32,340 --> 00:17:33,810
Get them out !

180
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:42,280
Michael, get out of the water !

181
00:17:52,790 --> 00:17:55,350
[ Man ] Take it easy. It's gonna be all right.

182
00:17:55,430 --> 00:17:56,660
Alex ?

183
00:17:57,730 --> 00:17:59,960
It's gonna be okay, now.

184
00:18:00,070 --> 00:18:01,290
Alex ?

185
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:15,170
[ Man ] Alex Kintner is the kid who was missing at the beach.

186
00:18:15,280 --> 00:18:17,840
We don't even know that there's a shark around here.

187
00:18:17,950 --> 00:18:19,650
I can't argue with you. I can't talk to you.

188
00:18:19,850 --> 00:18:22,150
I can't argue with you. I can't talk to you.

189
00:18:22,290 --> 00:18:25,220
I've got to talk to Mrs. Kintner because this is going to turn into a contest.

190
00:18:25,320 --> 00:18:28,290
It's not just the Gazette. She's advertised in out-of-town papers.

191
00:18:28,390 --> 00:18:30,890
People all over New England are gonna know about it.

192
00:18:31,030 --> 00:18:33,060
Let's go to council chambers where we'll have more room.

193
00:18:33,170 --> 00:18:35,430
I'm responsible for public safety.

194
00:18:35,540 --> 00:18:38,160
Then go see that no one gets hurt.

195
00:18:38,270 --> 00:18:40,240
Marty, do something about this. It's a small story.

196
00:18:40,340 --> 00:18:44,300
I'm gonna bury it as deep as I can... in back with the grocery ads.

197
00:18:44,410 --> 00:18:48,780
Right in here, please.

198
00:18:48,850 --> 00:18:50,510
Move on in, please.

199
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,590
Excuse me, please.

200
00:19:03,330 --> 00:19:06,630
Why do you insist on playing the heavy all the time ?

201
00:19:06,730 --> 00:19:10,130
I have a point of view and it speaks for many of the people here.

202
00:19:13,310 --> 00:19:16,300
It's not only me. How do you feel ? I hope they don't close beaches.

203
00:19:16,410 --> 00:19:20,980
Let's have some order.

204
00:19:21,010 --> 00:19:22,980
Let's have order, please.

205
00:19:24,420 --> 00:19:25,820
Any special questions ?

206
00:19:27,090 --> 00:19:30,580
Is that $3000 bounty on the shark in cash or check ? [ Laughing ]

207
00:19:31,820 --> 00:19:35,260
I don't think that's funny at all. I'm sorry.

208
00:19:36,330 --> 00:19:41,530
All right. All right ! That's private business between you fishermen and Mrs. Kintner.

209
00:19:42,370 --> 00:19:47,830
Martin ? Would you, please ? Chief Brody.

210
00:19:49,310 --> 00:19:53,470
I want to tell you what we're planning so far.

211
00:19:53,580 --> 00:19:55,310
What about the beaches ?

212
00:19:55,410 --> 00:19:59,850
We're gonna put on the extra summer deputies as soon as possible.

213
00:19:59,950 --> 00:20:03,410
Then we're gonna try and use shark spotters on the beach.

214
00:20:03,520 --> 00:20:05,720
Are you going to close the beaches ?

215
00:20:07,460 --> 00:20:10,090
Yes, we are.

216
00:20:12,830 --> 00:20:14,800
We're planning to bring in some experts

217
00:20:14,900 --> 00:20:16,700
from the oceanographic institute.

218
00:20:16,700 --> 00:20:19,730
Only 24 hours.

219
00:20:19,840 --> 00:20:21,570
I didn't agree to that.

220
00:20:23,940 --> 00:20:25,710
Only 24 hours.

221
00:20:25,810 --> 00:20:28,340
2 4 hours is like three weeks!

222
00:20:52,140 --> 00:20:54,200
You all know me,

223
00:20:54,310 --> 00:20:57,040
know how I earn a livin'.

224
00:20:57,140 --> 00:21:00,040
I'll catch this bird for you, but it ain't gonna be easy.

225
00:21:00,150 --> 00:21:02,080
Bad fish.

226
00:21:02,180 --> 00:21:05,450
Not like goin' down to the pond and chasin' bluegills or tommy-cods.

227
00:21:07,490 --> 00:21:09,720
This shark, swallow you whole.

228
00:21:10,920 --> 00:21:14,480
A little shakin', a little tenderizin',

229
00:21:14,590 --> 00:21:16,320
down you go.

230
00:21:16,430 --> 00:21:19,230
And we gotta do it quick. Gotta bring back the tourists.

231
00:21:19,330 --> 00:21:21,890
That'll put all your businesses on a payin' basis.

232
00:21:23,400 --> 00:21:25,670
But it's not gonna be pleasant !

233
00:21:25,770 --> 00:21:28,710
I value my neck a lot more than three thousand bucks, Chief.

234
00:21:29,710 --> 00:21:31,340
I'll find him for three,

235
00:21:31,440 --> 00:21:34,780
but I'll catch him and kill him for ten.

236
00:21:34,880 --> 00:21:37,310
You gotta make up your minds.

237
00:21:37,420 --> 00:21:39,320
Gonna stay alive and ante up, or gonna play it cheap ?

238
00:21:39,420 --> 00:21:44,390
Be on welfare the whole winter.

239
00:21:44,460 --> 00:21:46,890
I don't want no volunteers, no mates.

240
00:21:46,960 --> 00:21:49,020
There's too many captains on this island.

241
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:53,390
$ 1 0,000 for me, by myself.

242
00:21:53,500 --> 00:21:55,740
For that you get the head,

243
00:21:55,740 --> 00:21:59,300
the tail, the whole damn thing.

244
00:22:02,340 --> 00:22:04,330
Thank you very much, Mr. Quint.

245
00:22:05,980 --> 00:22:08,780
We'll take it under advisement.

246
00:22:11,850 --> 00:22:14,220
Mr. Mayor... Chief.

247
00:22:16,760 --> 00:22:18,380
Ladies and gentlemen.

248
00:22:51,690 --> 00:22:54,250
Oh, God ! You scared me.

249
00:22:55,690 --> 00:22:58,250
Oh.

250
00:22:58,400 --> 00:23:02,030
You know, Ellen, people don't even know how old sharks are.

251
00:23:02,130 --> 00:23:04,570
I mean, if they live two, three thousand years. Martin ?

252
00:23:04,670 --> 00:23:07,330
They don't know ! Enough, enough.

253
00:23:07,440 --> 00:23:10,000
You're not gonna be able to sleep tonight.

254
00:23:11,480 --> 00:23:15,040
Here, c'mon. Thanks.

255
00:23:23,220 --> 00:23:25,380
Wanna get drunk and fool around ?

256
00:23:25,520 --> 00:23:26,990
Oh yeah.

257
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:33,120
Hey, Mikey really loves his present.

258
00:23:34,600 --> 00:23:36,120
Where is he ?

259
00:23:36,240 --> 00:23:37,730
Sitting in it.

260
00:23:40,170 --> 00:23:42,330
Good God !

261
00:23:45,610 --> 00:23:47,580
All right, Michael, out of the boat !

262
00:23:47,680 --> 00:23:52,250
Tied up to the jetty, sittin' in the boat.

263
00:23:52,350 --> 00:23:53,820
Helpin' Michael.

264
00:23:53,920 --> 00:23:58,480
Get out of that boat ! Hi, Dad. Just a little longer, please ?

265
00:23:58,620 --> 00:24:00,820
It's his birthday tomorrow. I don't want him on the ocean.

266
00:24:00,960 --> 00:24:04,090
He's not on the ocean. He's in a boat. He's not gonna go in the water.

267
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:07,290
I don't think he'll ever go in the water again after what happened yesterday.

268
00:24:10,100 --> 00:24:11,660
All right, now don't say that.

269
00:24:12,770 --> 00:24:14,830
I don't want that to happen, you know that.

270
00:24:17,110 --> 00:24:19,100
But I want him to read the boating regulations, the rules,

271
00:24:19,210 --> 00:24:22,040
before he goes out on his own.

272
00:24:22,110 --> 00:24:25,110
Michael, did you hear your father ?

273
00:24:25,220 --> 00:24:27,810
Out of the water, now ! Now !

274
00:24:35,130 --> 00:24:38,100
I'm tired. Let's stop before someone reports us.

275
00:24:39,330 --> 00:24:41,990
Don't worry. The chief lives on the other side of the island.

276
00:24:43,170 --> 00:24:45,470
Am I comin' in straight ?

277
00:24:45,570 --> 00:24:47,060
Just keep rowin'.

278
00:24:56,020 --> 00:24:58,980
[ Man ] We'd better catch somethin'. This is my wife's holiday roast.

279
00:25:00,090 --> 00:25:03,280
Don't worry about it. $3000 buys an awful lot of roast.

280
00:25:11,100 --> 00:25:13,960
Come and get it !

281
00:25:17,870 --> 00:25:19,900
The tide's takin' it right out.

282
00:25:21,340 --> 00:25:24,400
Can't we go home ?

283
00:26:22,530 --> 00:26:29,300
Hey. Hey, he's takin' it ! He's takin' it ! - He's takin'it. - Hey, go ! Go !

284
00:26:29,310 --> 00:26:30,780
Go, go, go !

285
00:26:59,770 --> 00:27:02,470
Charlie, take my word for it ! Don't look back !

286
00:27:02,570 --> 00:27:05,130
Swim, Charlie, swim ! C'mon, Charlie, swim !

287
00:27:06,380 --> 00:27:10,150
Swim, Charlie, c'mon, to me, boy! C'mon, Charlie, swim to me!

288
00:27:10,150 --> 00:27:12,210
C'mon, keep swimmin'. Keep swimmin'.

289
00:27:12,280 --> 00:27:15,010
C'mon, a little more. Atta boy! Atta boy!

290
00:27:16,520 --> 00:27:18,650
[ Charlie ] I can't get up ! I can't get up !

291
00:27:18,790 --> 00:27:20,350
Give me your hand. C'mon. I can't get up.

292
00:27:20,490 --> 00:27:22,290
Help me !

293
00:27:22,430 --> 00:27:29,720
Help me ! Get your feet outta the water! Get your feet up. Atta boy! Atta boy, Charlie.

294
00:27:38,080 --> 00:27:39,810
Can we go home now ?

295
00:27:49,390 --> 00:27:49,620
[ Hendricks ] Then Denherder and Charlie sat there...

296
00:27:49,790 --> 00:27:53,330
[ Hendricks ] Then Denherder and Charlie sat there... tryin' to catch their breath, figurin' out how to tell Charlie's wife...

297
00:27:53,330 --> 00:27:57,300
what happened to her freezer full of meat.

298
00:27:57,300 --> 00:27:59,760
That's not funny at all !

299
00:27:59,870 --> 00:28:02,660
Mrs. Kintner must have put her ad in Field and Stream.

300
00:28:02,770 --> 00:28:04,860
Looks more like the National Enquirer.

301
00:28:06,270 --> 00:28:07,740
[ Arguing ]

302
00:28:07,740 --> 00:28:10,680
All right, hold it ! Just hold it !

303
00:28:16,650 --> 00:28:20,950
Hello. Hello back, young feller. How are you ?

304
00:28:20,950 --> 00:28:24,010
I hope you're not going out with those nuts, are you ?

305
00:28:28,890 --> 00:28:32,930
The Weetock boat's gotta move out first. You have to move out or he can't get out at all.

306
00:28:32,930 --> 00:28:35,830
Ahoy ! Don't raise sail. You're just gonna luff it.

307
00:28:35,930 --> 00:28:37,400
You got a paddle ? Scull it out of here. Yeah.

308
00:28:37,500 --> 00:28:41,370
Officer, wait a second. Wait. Just--

309
00:28:42,440 --> 00:28:45,970
Hey, how many guys you gonna put aboard that boat ?

310
00:28:46,080 --> 00:28:48,510
Whatever's safe, right ? Well, that ain't safe !

311
00:28:48,610 --> 00:28:50,670
Hey, watch it. That's dynamite.

312
00:28:50,780 --> 00:28:53,270
Wait a minute. Where are you going with that ?

313
00:28:53,390 --> 00:28:55,620
I'm goin' on the boat. Oh, no, no, no.

314
00:28:55,720 --> 00:28:57,990
Help me get those guys out of the boat, will you ?

315
00:28:58,120 --> 00:28:59,180
Sure.

316
00:28:59,320 --> 00:29:01,590
Gentlemen, the officer asked me to tell you...

317
00:29:01,690 --> 00:29:04,830
that you're overloading that boat.

318
00:29:04,830 --> 00:29:07,260
Ah, get out of here. Ah.

319
00:29:07,370 --> 00:29:09,390
You ain't going! What do you care ? Okay.

320
00:29:09,500 --> 00:29:12,600
Can you tell me if there's a restaurant or hotel on the island ?

321
00:29:12,700 --> 00:29:14,670
Yeah, you walk straight ahead.

322
00:29:14,940 --> 00:29:18,310
[ Laughing ] Ha-ha-ha. They're all gonna die.

323
00:29:18,380 --> 00:29:20,810
Polly, listen. We've got roadblock signs outside.

324
00:29:20,910 --> 00:29:23,810
You gotta get somebody to help us.

325
00:29:23,920 --> 00:29:26,610
Get those roadblock signs out on the highway,

326
00:29:26,720 --> 00:29:29,480
because we got more people down here than we can handle.

327
00:29:29,620 --> 00:29:31,750
- Yeah ? - What are you doing ?

328
00:29:31,890 --> 00:29:35,330
These are your people. Go and talk to them. Those aren't my people !

329
00:29:35,430 --> 00:29:37,330
They're from all over. Did you see the license plates ?

330
00:29:37,430 --> 00:29:39,900
Connecticut, Rhode Island, New Jersey.

331
00:29:40,030 --> 00:29:42,660
What happened to the extra help we're supposed to get ?

332
00:29:42,770 --> 00:29:45,290
That's not 'til the 4th of July. Until then, it's you and me.

333
00:29:45,400 --> 00:29:47,740
You know those eight guys on the fantail launch ? Yeah.

334
00:29:47,840 --> 00:29:50,330
None of them are gonna get out of the harbor alive.

335
00:29:50,440 --> 00:29:54,040
That's what I'm talkin' about. You know their first names. Talk to those clowns !

336
00:29:54,150 --> 00:29:56,710
Everyone seems to be having a good time today. Tell me about it !

337
00:29:56,820 --> 00:29:59,940
I'll get back to you. Could you tell me how I could find chief Brody ?

338
00:30:01,250 --> 00:30:02,550
Who are you ? Matt Hooper.

339
00:30:02,690 --> 00:30:05,380
I'm from the oceanographic institute.

340
00:30:05,520 --> 00:30:07,580
Oh, for Christ sakes. You're the guy we called.

341
00:30:07,730 --> 00:30:10,020
I'm Brody. Oh, I'm very glad to meet you.

342
00:30:10,130 --> 00:30:12,460
I'm glad to meet you too. I know you got a lot on your hands now, but --

343
00:30:12,560 --> 00:30:14,120
What can we do for you ?

344
00:30:14,230 --> 00:30:16,340
I think the best thing for me to do...

345
00:30:16,340 --> 00:30:21,830
is to see the remains of the first victim, the girl on the beach. Okay, fine,Just bear with me. Thanks. Sure.

346
00:30:22,880 --> 00:30:26,110
Wait'll we get them silly bastards down in that rock pile.

347
00:30:26,210 --> 00:30:29,270
They'll wish their fathers had never met their mothers...

348
00:30:29,380 --> 00:30:33,720
when they start diggin' their bottoms out and slammin' into them rocks.

349
00:30:33,750 --> 00:30:37,120
[ Man ] Get away from there, you goddamn fool!

350
00:30:37,260 --> 00:30:40,660
What's the matter with you ? You wanna swamp us you crazy son-of-a-bitch ?

351
00:30:40,760 --> 00:30:44,220
What are you doin' ? What are these guys doin' out here ?

352
00:30:44,360 --> 00:30:46,330
What the hell they doin' ?

353
00:30:46,430 --> 00:30:48,830
They're chummin' right now.Chumming ? What the hell is that ?

354
00:30:48,930 --> 00:30:50,330
They're tracking the shark.

355
00:30:50,440 --> 00:30:53,400
$3000 divided four ways is what ?

356
00:31:02,410 --> 00:31:04,710
Let's show Mr. Hooper our accident.

357
00:31:08,090 --> 00:31:10,080
''Victim identified as Christine Watkins, female Caucasian.''

358
00:31:10,190 --> 00:31:12,790
Here's the way we have it.

359
00:31:12,790 --> 00:31:15,090
''Probable boating accident.'' Yeah.

360
00:31:16,460 --> 00:31:17,830
All right ?

361
00:31:21,030 --> 00:31:23,060
The height and weight of the victim...

362
00:31:23,170 --> 00:31:25,660
can only be estimated from the partial remains.

363
00:31:27,170 --> 00:31:30,870
[ Breathing Deeply ]

364
00:31:31,040 --> 00:31:33,600
The torso has been severed in mid-thorax, no major organs remaining.

365
00:31:33,710 --> 00:31:36,680
May I have a glass of water ?

366
00:31:36,780 --> 00:31:39,950
The right arm has been severed above the elbow,

367
00:31:40,050 --> 00:31:43,080
with massive tissue loss in the upper musculature.

368
00:31:44,960 --> 00:31:46,290
Thank you, very much.

369
00:31:48,560 --> 00:31:51,290
Partially denuded bone remaining.

370
00:31:51,400 --> 00:31:53,330
This was no boat accident. Did you notify the Coast Guard about this ?

371
00:31:53,430 --> 00:31:56,920
No, it was only local jurisdiction.

372
00:32:00,010 --> 00:32:04,640
The left arm, head, shoulders, sternum and portions of the rib cage are intact.

373
00:32:04,740 --> 00:32:06,640
Do not smoke in here !

374
00:32:09,080 --> 00:32:10,480
This is what happens.

375
00:32:12,350 --> 00:32:15,320
It indicates the non-frenzied feeding of a large squalus,

376
00:32:15,450 --> 00:32:19,390
possibly Longimanus or Isurus glauca.

377
00:32:19,490 --> 00:32:22,790
Now... the enormous amount of tissue loss...

378
00:32:22,890 --> 00:32:24,690
prevents any detailed analysis.

379
00:32:24,800 --> 00:32:27,130
However, the attacking squalus must be considerably larger...

380
00:32:27,230 --> 00:32:30,430
than any normal squalus found in these waters.

381
00:32:30,540 --> 00:32:32,970
Didn't you get out a boat and check out these waters ? No.

382
00:32:33,070 --> 00:32:36,140
[ Hooper ] This is not a boat accident!

383
00:32:36,240 --> 00:32:39,770
It wasn't any propeller. It wasn't any coral reef.

384
00:32:39,880 --> 00:32:41,470
And it wasn't Jack the Ripper !

385
00:32:44,950 --> 00:32:46,440
It was a shark.

386
00:32:50,960 --> 00:32:52,690
[ Man ] You heard it.

387
00:32:56,830 --> 00:32:58,920
We brought it home!

388
00:33:00,930 --> 00:33:06,510
Listen, I wanna go AP and UPI. I wanna get on the state wire services.

389
00:33:06,510 --> 00:33:08,560
See if Boston'll pick it up.

390
00:33:08,640 --> 00:33:11,610
Call Dave Axelrod. Tell him he owes me a favor.

391
00:33:11,710 --> 00:33:14,680
This is the shot I want with everybody and the fish in it.

392
00:33:14,780 --> 00:33:17,420
[ Reporter ] Can we please get organized?

393
00:33:17,420 --> 00:33:19,650
I wanna get a picture for the paper.

394
00:33:19,750 --> 00:33:22,420
Ben Gardner get this ?

395
00:33:22,420 --> 00:33:24,550
[ Man ] No, no, no. We caught it.

396
00:33:24,690 --> 00:33:27,820
We got it. We got it.

397
00:33:27,960 --> 00:33:29,480
Hey, that's swell. That's a beauty, ain't it ?

398
00:33:30,460 --> 00:33:34,330
[ Reporter ] I need a picture for the paper. Clear out of the way, please.

399
00:33:34,430 --> 00:33:36,600
Just the guys who caught the fish.

400
00:33:36,600 --> 00:33:39,070
Could you open it up a little, please ?

401
00:33:39,070 --> 00:33:43,700
C'mon, guys, please. I need a picture for the paper.

402
00:33:43,810 --> 00:33:45,710
Could we get the ''beach closed'' sign ?

403
00:33:45,780 --> 00:33:48,870
[ Indistinct ]

404
00:33:54,250 --> 00:33:56,380
Young fellow, could you step out of the picture ?

405
00:33:58,790 --> 00:34:02,690
Get real. We're ready.

406
00:34:02,790 --> 00:34:04,260
- Can you get that, please ?

407
00:34:04,400 --> 00:34:06,560
- How's that ?

408
00:34:08,830 --> 00:34:10,170
Larry !

409
00:34:11,940 --> 00:34:13,700
Larry, you won't believe it.

410
00:34:13,810 --> 00:34:15,670
What kind of a shark is it ? I don't know.

411
00:34:15,770 --> 00:34:19,610
I think it's a mako. It's got a deep throat.

412
00:34:19,610 --> 00:34:21,410
- Yeah, but what kind of shark ?

413
00:34:21,510 --> 00:34:23,340
- Tiger shark.

414
00:34:23,450 --> 00:34:26,080
A what ?

415
00:34:26,150 --> 00:34:29,020
We can start breathing again.

416
00:34:29,150 --> 00:34:30,120
Ben getting plenty of pictures ? You bet he is.

417
00:34:30,220 --> 00:34:33,190
What is this ''bite radius'' crap ? That is a big mouth !

418
00:34:33,330 --> 00:34:38,160
Stuff your head in there and find out if it's a man-eater !

419
00:34:42,470 --> 00:34:44,590
All I'm saying is that it may not be the shark.

420
00:34:44,700 --> 00:34:47,100
It's just a slight -- Matt ?

421
00:34:47,210 --> 00:34:50,310
This is Larry Vaughn, our mayor. Hi.

422
00:34:50,310 --> 00:34:52,440
Matt's from the oceanographic institute. Nice to meet you.

423
00:34:52,540 --> 00:34:55,140
Terrific, huh, Mayor ?

424
00:34:55,250 --> 00:34:58,740
Martin, there are all kinds of sharks in the waters;

425
00:34:58,850 --> 00:35:01,340
hammerheads, white tips, blues, makos.

426
00:35:01,450 --> 00:35:03,580
The chances these bozos got the exact shark --

427
00:35:03,720 --> 00:35:06,120
There's no other shark like this in these waters.

428
00:35:06,220 --> 00:35:08,620
It's a hundred to one... a hundred to one.

429
00:35:08,730 --> 00:35:12,960
I'm not saying this is not the shark. It probably is.

430
00:35:13,060 --> 00:35:15,730
It's a man-eater. It's extremely rare for these waters.

431
00:35:15,830 --> 00:35:18,130
But the fact is that the bite radius on this animal...

432
00:35:18,240 --> 00:35:20,500
is different than the wounds on the victim.

433
00:35:22,510 --> 00:35:25,070
I just -- I wanna be sure.

434
00:35:25,180 --> 00:35:28,280
You wanna be sure. We all wanna be sure, okay ? What I want to do is simple.

435
00:35:28,280 --> 00:35:32,510
The digestive system of this animal is very slow.

436
00:35:32,620 --> 00:35:35,780
Whatever it's eaten in the last 24 hours is bound to still be in there.

437
00:35:35,920 --> 00:35:37,680
Then we'll be sure.

438
00:35:43,930 --> 00:35:45,990
It may be the only way to confirm it, huh ?

439
00:35:46,100 --> 00:35:48,790
Look, fellas, let's be reasonable, huh ?

440
00:35:48,930 --> 00:35:51,300
This is not the time or place to perform ...

441
00:35:51,400 --> 00:35:55,810
some kind of half-assed autopsy on a fish.

442
00:35:55,810 --> 00:35:57,870
I'm not going to stand here and see that thing cut open...

443
00:35:57,980 --> 00:36:05,050
and see that Kintner boy spill out all over the dock !

444
00:36:16,360 --> 00:36:19,920
Chief Brody ? Yes ?

445
00:36:27,940 --> 00:36:29,500
I just found out...

446
00:36:31,180 --> 00:36:33,440
that a girl got killed here last week.

447
00:36:35,250 --> 00:36:36,680
And you knew it !

448
00:36:37,950 --> 00:36:40,080
You knew there was a shark out there.

449
00:36:41,820 --> 00:36:44,860
You knew it was dangerous.

450
00:36:44,960 --> 00:36:47,550
But you let people go swimming anyway.

451
00:36:52,030 --> 00:36:54,020
You knew all those things,

452
00:36:56,230 --> 00:37:00,690
but still my boy is dead now.

453
00:37:04,410 --> 00:37:06,640
And there's nothing you can do about it.

454
00:37:12,980 --> 00:37:14,950
My boy is dead.

455
00:37:20,230 --> 00:37:22,190
I wanted you to know that.

456
00:37:34,810 --> 00:37:39,780
I'm sorry, Martin. She's wrong.

457
00:37:39,780 --> 00:37:41,180
No, she's not.

458
00:37:46,650 --> 00:37:48,380
[ Vaughn ] All right, fellas,

459
00:37:48,490 --> 00:37:51,960
let's cut this ugly son-of-a-bitch down... before it stinks up the whole island.

460
00:37:51,960 --> 00:37:54,860
Harve, you and Carl take it out tomorrow and dump it in the drink.

461
00:39:07,630 --> 00:39:09,000
Come here.

462
00:39:12,340 --> 00:39:14,310
Give us a kiss.

463
00:39:14,410 --> 00:39:15,700
Why ?

464
00:39:17,410 --> 00:39:19,600
Because I need it.

465
00:39:23,580 --> 00:39:25,520
Hello. Get out of here.

466
00:39:27,150 --> 00:39:29,420
[ Ellen ] Can I help you ? Mind if I come in ?

467
00:39:29,550 --> 00:39:32,520
I'm Matt Hooper. Hi. Ellen Brody.

468
00:39:32,620 --> 00:39:35,250
Your husband's home ? I'd like to talk to him. Yes.

469
00:39:35,390 --> 00:39:37,360
Yes, so would I.

470
00:39:38,560 --> 00:39:40,550
Come in. Can I get you some coffee ? No, nothing, thank you.

471
00:39:40,670 --> 00:39:44,660
Oh, wine. How nice.

472
00:40:02,690 --> 00:40:04,150
How was your day ?

473
00:40:10,160 --> 00:40:11,530
Swell.

474
00:40:12,830 --> 00:40:14,420
Yeah. I got red and white.

475
00:40:14,530 --> 00:40:20,140
I didn't know what you'd be serving. Oh, that's nice.

476
00:40:20,210 --> 00:40:22,230
Is anyone eating this ?

477
00:40:23,070 --> 00:40:24,230
No.

478
00:40:31,680 --> 00:40:33,780
My husband tells me you're in sharks.

479
00:40:35,250 --> 00:40:40,050
[ Hooper Laughing ] Excuse me, well, yes. I've never heard it quite put that way,

480
00:40:40,190 --> 00:40:43,160
but yes, I am. I love sharks.

481
00:40:43,260 --> 00:40:46,230
You love sharks. Yeah, I love them.

482
00:40:46,330 --> 00:40:48,390
When I was twelve, my father got me this boat

483
00:40:48,500 --> 00:40:50,470
and I went fishing off Cape Cod.

484
00:40:50,570 --> 00:40:52,540
I hooked a scup and as I was reeling it in,

485
00:40:52,640 --> 00:40:58,310
I hooked a 4-and-a-half foot baby thresher shark, who proceeded to eat my boat. [ Laughing ]

486
00:40:58,440 --> 00:41:01,940
He ate my oar, hooks, and my seat cushions.

487
00:41:02,050 --> 00:41:05,110
He turned an inboard into an outboard. Scared me to death.

488
00:41:05,220 --> 00:41:07,080
And I swam back to shore.

489
00:41:07,190 --> 00:41:09,380
When I was on the beach, I turned around...

490
00:41:09,520 --> 00:41:11,580
and actually saw my boat being taken apart.

491
00:41:11,720 --> 00:41:14,190
Ever since then, yes, I have been studying sharks.

492
00:41:14,290 --> 00:41:17,850
That's why I know that I'm going to go to the institute tomorrow...

493
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:20,620
and tell them that you still have a shark problem here.

494
00:41:20,730 --> 00:41:23,360
Why do you have to tell them that ? Sorry.

495
00:41:23,470 --> 00:41:25,870
I'm sorry. You told me the shark was caught.

496
00:41:25,970 --> 00:41:28,440
I heard it on the news, on the cape station.

497
00:41:28,540 --> 00:41:31,630
They caught a shark, not the shark.

498
00:41:31,740 --> 00:41:33,840
Not the shark that killed Chrissie Watkins;

499
00:41:33,950 --> 00:41:37,310
and probably not the shark that killed the little boy,

500
00:41:37,420 --> 00:41:39,780
which I wanted to prove by cutting the shark open.

501
00:41:39,880 --> 00:41:42,550
You want to let that breath -- ? Nothing.

502
