752
01:04:07,450 --> 01:04:11,610
Doctor said he's okay. Mild shock. He can go home in the morning. Thank you.

753
01:04:12,630 --> 01:04:15,060
Hey, how's my big kid ? I'm all right.

754
01:04:15,160 --> 01:04:18,060
You are. You gonna miss me tonight ?

755
01:04:18,160 --> 01:04:20,800
You can watch TV. Want me to bring you anything from home ? My cars. Your cars. What about ice cream ?

756
01:04:20,800 --> 01:04:23,770
Coffee. Coffee.

757
01:04:35,210 --> 01:04:37,110
Want to take him home ?

758
01:04:39,150 --> 01:04:41,020
Like to New York ?

759
01:04:41,120 --> 01:04:43,710
No, home here.

760
01:05:01,910 --> 01:05:05,170
I'm sorry. I'm truly sorry.

761
01:05:05,280 --> 01:05:07,640
Got a pen, Larry ? Pen ?

762
01:05:07,750 --> 01:05:09,510
Yeah, pen, you know.

763
01:05:12,820 --> 01:05:14,980
'Cause you're gonna do what you do best.

764
01:05:15,090 --> 01:05:17,890
You're gonna sign this voucher so I can hire a contractor.

765
01:05:18,020 --> 01:05:19,920
I don't know if I can do that without--

766
01:05:20,030 --> 01:05:22,820
I'm gonna hire Quint to kill the shark.

767
01:05:23,700 --> 01:05:25,890
[ Mumbling ] August. What ?

768
01:05:26,000 --> 01:05:28,760
What are you talking about ? Summer is over.

769
01:05:28,870 --> 01:05:32,360
You're the mayor of Shark City. These people think you want the beaches open.

770
01:05:32,470 --> 01:05:36,030
I was acting in the town's best interest.

771
01:05:36,140 --> 01:05:39,740
You were, and that's why you're gonna do the right thing.

772
01:05:39,850 --> 01:05:43,470
Sign this and pay that guy what he wants. Martin.

773
01:05:44,850 --> 01:05:47,080
Martin.

774
01:05:48,620 --> 01:05:51,610
My kids were on that beach too.

775
01:06:02,100 --> 01:06:03,630
Sign it, Larry.

776
01:06:12,010 --> 01:06:16,810
[ Quint ] $ 1 0,000. $ 200 a day whether I catch him or not.

777
01:06:16,920 --> 01:06:18,140
[ Brody ] You've got it.

778
01:06:18,250 --> 01:06:21,340
Get the mayor off my back so I don't have any more of this zoning crap.

779
01:06:21,450 --> 01:06:22,890
You've got that.

780
01:06:22,990 --> 01:06:26,990
One case of apricot brandy. You buy the lunch.

781
01:06:26,990 --> 01:06:30,220
Two cases. You get dinner when you get back.

782
01:06:30,330 --> 01:06:33,630
[ Quint ] Champagne, pate de foie gras, Iranian caviar...

783
01:06:33,730 --> 01:06:36,760
and don't forget the color TV.

784
01:06:38,370 --> 01:06:41,360
Hey, Chief, try this. Made it myself. Pretty good stuff.

785
01:06:41,470 --> 01:06:44,910
Thanks.

786
01:06:44,910 --> 01:06:47,710
[ Quint ] Here's to swimmin' with bowlegged women.

787
01:06:55,090 --> 01:06:56,880
[ Indistinct Noise ] Excuse me, Chief.

788
01:07:10,870 --> 01:07:14,460
[ Quint ] Can't get a good man these days under 60.

789
01:07:14,570 --> 01:07:16,910
All gone at least 35 years.

790
01:07:16,910 --> 01:07:19,780
Don't drink that. [ Quint Mumbling ]

791
01:07:19,780 --> 01:07:25,570
Mr. Quint ? Mr. Quint ? Mr. Quint, you're gonna need an extra hand.

792
01:07:25,680 --> 01:07:27,240
This is Matt Hooper. I know who he is.

793
01:07:27,350 --> 01:07:30,220
I've crewed three trans-pacs. Transplants ?

794
01:07:30,320 --> 01:07:32,810
He's from the oceanographic institute. An America's Cup trial.

795
01:07:32,960 --> 01:07:37,760
I'm not talkin' about pleasure boatin' or day sailin'.

796
01:07:37,860 --> 01:07:41,990
I'm talkin'about workin' for a livin', sharkin'.

797
01:07:42,100 --> 01:07:45,230
I'm not talking about hooking some dogfish or sand shark.

798
01:07:45,340 --> 01:07:48,470
I'm talking about finding a great white.

799
01:07:48,570 --> 01:07:51,410
Porkers ? Talking about porkers, Mr. Hooper ?

800
01:07:54,850 --> 01:07:57,080
Tie me a sheepshank.

801
01:07:59,550 --> 01:08:02,710
[ Sighing ] I haven't had to pass basic seamanship in a long time.

802
01:08:03,860 --> 01:08:06,260
You didn't say how short you wanted it.

803
01:08:08,960 --> 01:08:10,450
How's that ?

804
01:08:13,830 --> 01:08:15,390
Give me your hands.

805
01:08:16,900 --> 01:08:18,370
Dogfish ?

806
01:08:18,470 --> 01:08:22,910
You got a $5,000 net and $2,000 worth of fish.

807
01:08:23,010 --> 01:08:25,500
Along comes Mr. Whitey. By the time he's finished with that net...

808
01:08:25,610 --> 01:08:29,170
it looks like a kiddie's scissors class cut it up for a paper doll.

809
01:08:29,250 --> 01:08:34,110
You got city hands. You've been countin' money all your life.

810
01:08:34,220 --> 01:08:38,160
All right, all right ! I don't need this ! I don't need this working-class hero crap.

811
01:08:38,160 --> 01:08:42,290
You're not gonna do this aboard the ship, are you ?

812
01:08:42,390 --> 01:08:45,990
Maybe I should go alone.

813
01:08:48,730 --> 01:08:50,900
It's my party. It's my charter.

814
01:08:51,000 --> 01:08:54,300
Yeah, it's your charter. It's my vessel !

815
01:08:54,410 --> 01:08:56,270
When you're on board my vessel, I'm mate, master,

816
01:08:56,380 --> 01:09:00,210
pilot and I'm captain.

817
01:09:02,810 --> 01:09:05,970
Take him for ballast, Chief.

818
01:09:08,550 --> 01:09:09,950
You got him.

819
01:09:17,530 --> 01:09:19,460
Pliers, iron.

820
01:09:19,530 --> 01:09:22,690
[ Hooper ] Sample bottles, dye marker, flares, safety float,

821
01:09:22,800 --> 01:09:25,530
temperature gauge, spear gun, SMG--

822
01:09:25,670 --> 01:09:28,730
What are ya, some kind of half-assed astronaut ?

823
01:09:37,420 --> 01:09:41,110
[ Quint ] Take that stuff below and lash it secure.

824
01:09:45,920 --> 01:09:48,390
Jesus H. Christ.

825
01:09:48,490 --> 01:09:54,000
When I was a boy, every squirt wanted to be... a harpooner or swordfisherman.

826
01:09:54,000 --> 01:09:57,300
What you got here ? A portable shower or monkey cage ?

827
01:09:57,400 --> 01:09:58,800
Anti-shark cage.

828
01:09:58,900 --> 01:10:01,270
Anti-shark cage.

829
01:10:01,370 --> 01:10:03,240
You go inside the cage ?

830
01:10:05,780 --> 01:10:09,040
Cage goes in the water ? You go in the water ?

831
01:10:09,150 --> 01:10:12,710
Shark's in the water ? Our shark ?

832
01:10:14,720 --> 01:10:19,950
# Farewell and adieu to you fair Spanish ladies #

833
01:10:20,090 --> 01:10:24,690
# Farewell and adieu you ladies of Spain #

834
01:10:24,830 --> 01:10:27,560
# For we've received orders  #

835
01:10:27,670 --> 01:10:31,030
for to sail back to Boston

836
01:10:31,140 --> 01:10:35,900
And so nevermore shall we see you again

837
01:10:42,380 --> 01:10:45,440
Did you take your Dramamine ? Yes.

838
01:10:45,550 --> 01:10:48,820
I put an extra pair of glasses in your black socks.

839
01:10:48,920 --> 01:10:53,490
There's the stuff for your nose, the zinc oxide, and Blistex is in the kit.

840
01:10:53,490 --> 01:10:54,890
[ Quint ] Son of a bitch !

841
01:10:55,990 --> 01:10:58,460
Goddamn women today can't handle nothin'.

842
01:10:58,560 --> 01:11:02,020
Young girls ain't smart like their grandmothers.

843
01:11:02,170 --> 01:11:04,140
That's got to be Quint. Colorful, isn't he ?

844
01:11:04,240 --> 01:11:09,370
He scares me.

845
01:11:09,370 --> 01:11:11,500
Don't use the fireplace. I haven't fixed the flue yet.

846
01:11:11,610 --> 01:11:13,640
What am I gonna tell the kids ?

847
01:11:16,720 --> 01:11:18,950
Tell 'em I'm going fishing.

848
01:11:23,660 --> 01:11:29,730
[ Quint ] Break it up, will ya, Chief? Daylight's wastin'.

849
01:11:29,730 --> 01:11:32,060
Front, bow. back, stern. Don't get it right, squirt,

850
01:11:32,160 --> 01:11:36,870
I'll throw your ass out the round window on the side!

851
01:11:36,870 --> 01:11:40,500
Come on, Chief, this isn't a picnic.

852
01:11:40,610 --> 01:11:42,510
See ya got your rubbers. [ Laughing ]

853
01:11:44,880 --> 01:11:47,140
Here lies the body of Mary Lee.

854
01:11:47,250 --> 01:11:49,410
Died at the age of 1 03.

855
01:11:49,510 --> 01:11:52,350
For 1 5 years she kept her virginity,

856
01:11:52,450 --> 01:11:55,250
not a bad record for this vicinity.

857
01:11:55,350 --> 01:11:58,150
All right, Commissioner, fasten your safety belts.

858
01:12:00,290 --> 01:12:02,690
If you see a shark, Hooper, swallow.

859
01:12:06,900 --> 01:12:09,490
[ Quint ] Up periscope. Rig for depth charge.

860
01:12:09,600 --> 01:12:11,500
Stand by... fire drill.

861
01:12:17,040 --> 01:12:22,110
You know what I'm talkin'about, Chief? How's the missus, Chief?

862
01:12:22,150 --> 01:12:25,510
If they don't like you goin' out, they'll love you comin' in.

863
01:12:28,090 --> 01:12:32,920
# Oh, yo, ho, ho and a bottle of rum #

864
01:12:33,060 --> 01:12:36,320
# Fifteen men on the dead man's chest #

865
01:12:51,310 --> 01:12:54,770
Keep that chum line goin'. We got five miles on him.

866
01:12:55,780 --> 01:13:01,290
Who's driving this boat ? Nobody, the tide.

867
01:13:01,290 --> 01:13:03,580
One time I got a 1 6-footer off Montauk.

868
01:13:03,690 --> 01:13:07,180
Had to stick two barrels in him to wear him down and bring him up.

869
01:13:08,530 --> 01:13:10,960
Nowadays these kids take out everything.

870
01:13:11,060 --> 01:13:13,120
Radar, sonar,

871
01:13:13,270 --> 01:13:15,260
electric toothbrushes.

872
01:13:17,440 --> 01:13:19,670
Jesus H. Christ.

873
01:13:19,770 --> 01:13:23,140
Hey, Chief, best drop another chum marker.

874
01:13:46,000 --> 01:13:47,790
[ Hooper ] Damn it, Martin !

875
01:13:47,900 --> 01:13:50,130
This is compressed air.

876
01:13:50,240 --> 01:13:53,360
What the hell kind of a knot was that ? You pulled the wrong one !

877
01:13:53,470 --> 01:13:56,870
You screw around with these tanks and they're gonna blow up.

878
01:13:56,980 --> 01:14:00,710
Yeah, real fine, expensive gear you brought out here.

879
01:14:02,150 --> 01:14:04,550
But I don't know what that shark's gonna do with it.

880
01:14:04,650 --> 01:14:08,680
Might eat it, I suppose. Seen one eat a rockin' chair.

881
01:14:10,920 --> 01:14:12,550
Hey, Chiefy, next time,

882
01:14:12,690 --> 01:14:15,820
just ask me which line to pull, right ?

883
01:14:21,700 --> 01:14:24,260
[ Quint ] Little brown eel comes out of the cave,

884
01:14:25,370 --> 01:14:27,270
swims into the hole,

885
01:14:28,610 --> 01:14:31,080
comes out of the hole, goes back to the cave again.

886
01:14:32,840 --> 01:14:34,740
Not too good, is it, Chief?

887
01:14:34,850 --> 01:14:38,780
Well, nothing's easy, is it ? One more time.

888
01:15:09,880 --> 01:15:13,840
[ Brody ] The brown eel comes out of the cave.

889
01:15:57,930 --> 01:15:59,830
Hey ! I got it !

890
01:16:02,200 --> 01:16:04,570
What ? Get behind me !

891
01:16:07,770 --> 01:16:10,300
[ Quint ] Hooper, reverse her!

892
01:16:10,410 --> 01:16:12,400
Takin' a hell of a lot of line !

893
01:16:12,510 --> 01:16:15,600
Chief, get the scoop. Wet the reel !

894
01:16:19,550 --> 01:16:22,080
Hooper, reverse her !

895
01:16:25,690 --> 01:16:29,220
Duck your head down. We're swinging. Get behind me again.

896
01:16:29,360 --> 01:16:31,800
No more water. Don't drown me.

897
01:16:32,760 --> 01:16:36,530
Hooper, you idiot ! Starboard ! Ain't you watchin' it ?

898
01:16:40,110 --> 01:16:42,130
[ Quint ] Hooper, neutral.

899
01:16:48,780 --> 01:16:51,150
Where's he goin' now ?

900
01:16:51,250 --> 01:16:53,180
He ain't foolin' me.

901
01:16:54,120 --> 01:16:56,280
What's he yankin' on now ?

902
01:16:57,190 --> 01:16:58,920
Go on. Try it.

903
01:17:11,300 --> 01:17:14,290
I don't know, Chief. He's very smart or very dumb.

904
01:17:21,150 --> 01:17:23,770
Jesus Chr--

905
01:17:26,220 --> 01:17:28,690
He's gone under. Gone under the boat.

906
01:17:28,790 --> 01:17:30,810
I think he's gone under the boat.

907
01:17:32,560 --> 01:17:34,080
Yeah, it's too easy.

908
01:17:34,230 --> 01:17:37,990
He ain't a smart, big fish. He's gone under the boat.

909
01:17:38,100 --> 01:17:41,550
Keep it steady now. I got somethin' very big.

910
01:17:41,700 --> 01:17:43,100
I don't think so.

911
01:17:43,200 --> 01:17:46,430
Chief, Chief, put your gloves on.

912
01:17:46,540 --> 01:17:49,030
Put your gloves on, both of ya.

913
01:17:52,110 --> 01:17:54,700
Gettin'ready to run out again.

914
01:17:54,810 --> 01:17:56,510
Quint, let it go.

915
01:17:56,610 --> 01:18:00,310
You may be a big yahoo in the lab, but here you're just supercargo.

916
01:18:00,420 --> 01:18:02,650
If you don't want to backstroke home, get down here.

917
01:18:02,750 --> 01:18:05,590
All right, you don't want to listen to me, don't.

918
01:18:06,220 --> 01:18:07,660
It's not a shark.

919
01:18:07,760 --> 01:18:10,750
The wire's showing. The wire's showing ! Unbuckle me.

920
01:18:12,460 --> 01:18:16,560
Get the other side. It's tuna or swordfish.

921
01:18:16,670 --> 01:18:18,660
Wastin' our time.

922
01:18:18,770 --> 01:18:22,330
Okay, take this rod. Give the chief a hand.

923
01:18:22,440 --> 01:18:24,910
Right ! Oh, shit !

924
01:18:33,990 --> 01:18:37,650
It may be a marlin or a stingray,

925
01:18:37,760 --> 01:18:39,750
but it's definitely a game fish. Ohh--

926
01:18:51,900 --> 01:18:53,800
Gamin' fish, eh ? Marlin, stingray ?

927
01:18:53,910 --> 01:18:57,240
Bit through this piano wire ? Don't tell me my business.

928
01:18:57,240 --> 01:18:59,970
Get back on the bridge.

929
01:19:00,080 --> 01:19:02,880
Doesn't prove a thing.

930
01:19:02,980 --> 01:19:05,250
It proves one thing.

931
01:19:05,350 --> 01:19:07,250
It proves you wealthy college boys don't have the education...

932
01:19:07,350 --> 01:19:10,220
to admit when you're wrong.

933
01:19:19,930 --> 01:19:22,830
What's the point ? Hooks and lines ?

934
01:19:25,140 --> 01:19:27,800
Well, you lose one, you rig one.

935
01:19:28,970 --> 01:19:34,440
[ Engine Starting ] Hooper ! Twelve minutes, south southeast, full throttle.

936
01:19:34,550 --> 01:19:36,450
Aye, aye, sir. [ Grumbling ]

937
01:19:38,150 --> 01:19:41,740
See what I do, Chief, is trick 'em to the surface.

938
01:19:41,850 --> 01:19:43,790
I jab at 'em. I'm not gonna haul 'em up like catfish.

939
01:19:43,890 --> 01:19:47,460
Hooper !

940
01:19:47,460 --> 01:19:49,450
Full throttle!

941
01:19:49,590 --> 01:19:51,990
I don't have to take this abuse much longer.

942
01:19:52,100 --> 01:19:55,290
Your head's bleedin'. First aid there.

943
01:20:22,030 --> 01:20:25,930
Brody, start that chum line again, will ya ?

944
01:20:28,870 --> 01:20:30,770
Let Hooper take a turn.

945
01:20:30,870 --> 01:20:33,890
Hooper drives the boat.

946
01:20:48,550 --> 01:20:53,150
Stop playin' with yourself. Slow ahead, if you please.

947
01:20:53,290 --> 01:20:55,320
Ya heard him. Slow ahead.

948
01:21:04,300 --> 01:21:06,830
Slow ahead.

949
01:21:06,940 --> 01:21:09,500
I can go slow ahead. Come on down and chum some of this shit.

950
01:21:27,360 --> 01:21:29,290
You're gonna need a bigger boat.

951
01:21:42,810 --> 01:21:45,910
Shut off that engine !

952
01:22:14,340 --> 01:22:15,900
- That's a twenty-footer. - Twenty-five.

953
01:22:16,010 --> 01:22:19,410
Three tons of him.

954
01:22:25,180 --> 01:22:27,850
We're gonna need a bigger boat, right ?

955
01:22:27,950 --> 01:22:29,480
Gotta get to work. How do we handle this ?

956
01:22:29,590 --> 01:22:34,490
[ Hooper ] Come front. I need you.

957
01:22:36,060 --> 01:22:38,550
[ Hooper ] He's circling the boat.

958
01:22:40,130 --> 01:22:43,530
Come on, Martin.

959
01:22:49,170 --> 01:22:55,080
[ Radio ] Amity light station to Orca. This is Amity light station to Orca. Come in, Orca.

960
01:22:55,080 --> 01:22:58,650
Orca. Come in.

961
01:22:58,650 --> 01:23:01,640
I have Mrs. Martin Brody here. Put her on.

962
01:23:01,750 --> 01:23:05,780
[ Hooper ] Go on, Martin, move, move! I'm not going out there!

963
01:23:05,920 --> 01:23:09,260
Beyond the barrels, go to the end of the barrels.

964
01:23:09,360 --> 01:23:10,760
Further out ! What ?

965
01:23:10,860 --> 01:23:12,260
Go further out ! What for ?

966
01:23:12,360 --> 01:23:14,300
Go further out ! What for ?

967
01:23:14,400 --> 01:23:17,300
Will you go to the end of the pulpit, please ? What ?

968
01:23:17,400 --> 01:23:20,740
What for ? I need something in the foreground to give it scale.

969
01:23:20,840 --> 01:23:22,240
Foreground, my ass !

970
01:23:22,340 --> 01:23:25,370
Your husband's all right. He's fishing. Just caught a couple of stripers.

971
01:23:25,480 --> 01:23:29,440
We're bringin' dinner. We haven't seen anything. Over. Out.

972
01:23:29,550 --> 01:23:31,850
I'm not staying here. I'm begging you.

973
01:23:31,950 --> 01:23:35,390
Martin, goddamn it ! Come here, darlin', come here !

974
01:23:35,520 --> 01:23:36,920
[ Hooper ] Beautiful!

975
01:23:40,690 --> 01:23:44,320
Chief, get on the bridge. Take her forward, steady.

976
01:23:44,460 --> 01:23:47,090
I've never steered a boat in my life.

977
01:23:47,200 --> 01:23:49,060
Watch my hand. Take her steady.

978
01:23:49,170 --> 01:23:51,730
Mr. Hooper, attach the end of this line to the first keg.

979
01:23:53,200 --> 01:23:55,930
I've got to get a good shot at that porker's head.

980
01:24:10,290 --> 01:24:11,690
Comin',

981
01:24:12,720 --> 01:24:14,280
comin'.

982
01:24:14,430 --> 01:24:16,520
Hooper, get clear of the barrel.

983
01:24:18,000 --> 01:24:18,760
Hooper !

984
01:24:21,430 --> 01:24:24,370
Tie it up, will ya ? Your turn, Quint.

985
01:24:24,470 --> 01:24:26,030
Hooper, where are ya ?

986
01:24:28,470 --> 01:24:31,600
Hooper, hurry it up now. Tie it on.

987
01:24:33,380 --> 01:24:37,570
Hurry up, he's comin' straight for us. Don't screw it up. Don't wait for me !

988
01:24:39,150 --> 01:24:40,880
Come on, Hooper,

989
01:24:40,990 --> 01:24:43,450
Hurry up ! Tie it on !

990
01:24:43,590 --> 01:24:45,520
Now. Now.

991
01:24:48,390 --> 01:24:50,590
[ Brody ] Kill him, Quint. Kill him !

992
01:24:50,730 --> 01:24:51,700
Now !

993
01:24:53,800 --> 01:24:54,700
- Shoot ! - [ Gunshot ]

994
01:24:58,300 --> 01:24:59,700
Time !

995
01:24:59,800 --> 01:25:01,330
[ Quint ] What were you doin' ? I didn't get a clean shot in the head.

996
01:25:01,370 --> 01:25:04,860
[ Quint ] What were you doin' ? I didn't get a clean shot in the head.

997
01:25:04,980 --> 01:25:08,810
All right, let's see how long that barrel takes to bring him up.

998
01:25:09,450 --> 01:25:14,250
Free another barrel. I'm coming around again.

999
01:26:08,070 --> 01:26:10,110
What do we do now ? We're quitting, right ?

1000
01:26:10,110 --> 01:26:13,810
[ Quint ] We've got one barrel on him. We stay until we find him again.

1001
01:26:13,810 --> 01:26:15,870
We could radio in and get a bigger boat--

1002
01:26:38,570 --> 01:26:40,800
Chief.

1003
01:26:40,910 --> 01:26:43,470
Don't you worry about it, Chief.

1004
01:26:43,570 --> 01:26:46,580
It won't be permanent.

1005
01:26:46,580 --> 01:26:49,240
Want to see something permanent, boom, boom, boom ?

1006
01:26:53,720 --> 01:26:55,120
Hey, Hoop,

1007
01:26:55,220 --> 01:26:59,120
you wanna feel something permanent ?

1008
01:26:59,260 --> 01:27:03,360
Just put your hand underneath my cap. Feel that little lump ?

1009
01:27:03,360 --> 01:27:06,690
Knocko Nolans, St. Paddy's Day, Boston.

1010
01:27:10,840 --> 01:27:12,390
I got that beat.

1011
01:27:14,240 --> 01:27:15,830
I got that beat.

1012
01:27:20,340 --> 01:27:22,540
That's a moray eel.

1013
01:27:22,610 --> 01:27:24,980
Bit right through my wet suit.

1014
01:27:25,080 --> 01:27:27,050
Hoop, now, listen, I don't know about that,

1015
01:27:27,150 --> 01:27:30,250
but I entered an arm wrestling contest...

1016
01:27:30,350 --> 01:27:32,620
in an Okie bar in San Francisco.

1017
01:27:32,760 --> 01:27:35,120
I can't extend that, you know why ?

1018
01:27:35,260 --> 01:27:39,660
I was in the semifinal, celebratin' my wife's demise.

1019
01:27:39,760 --> 01:27:42,320
Big Chinese fella pulled me right over.

1020
01:27:55,280 --> 01:27:56,840
Look at that.

1021
01:27:58,250 --> 01:28:00,440
It was a bull shark.

1022
01:28:00,550 --> 01:28:03,650
He scraped me when I was takin' samples.

1023
01:28:03,790 --> 01:28:07,950
I got somethin' for ya. There's a thresher. See that, Chief?

1024
01:28:08,090 --> 01:28:09,790
Thresher's tail.

1025
01:28:09,930 --> 01:28:11,390
Thresher ?

1026
01:28:11,500 --> 01:28:13,860
It's a shark.

1027
01:28:14,930 --> 01:28:16,830
You want a drink ? Drink to your leg ?

1028
01:28:16,930 --> 01:28:19,960
I'll drink to your leg. Okay, we drink to our legs.

1029
01:28:25,340 --> 01:28:27,240
[ Hooper ] I got the creme de la creme.

1030
01:28:27,340 --> 01:28:29,780
Right here.

1031
01:28:29,880 --> 01:28:31,750
See that ?

1032
01:28:31,850 --> 01:28:34,410
[ Brody ] You're wearin' a sweater.

1033
01:28:34,520 --> 01:28:37,320
Right there. Mary Ellen Moffit.

1034
01:28:38,060 --> 01:28:39,960
She broke my heart. [ Laughing ]

1035
01:28:50,070 --> 01:28:52,760
What's that one ? [ Quint ] What ?

1036
01:28:52,870 --> 01:28:55,570
That one there on your arm.

1037
01:28:55,670 --> 01:28:58,640
Oh, a tattoo. I got that removed.

1038
01:28:58,740 --> 01:29:04,910
Don't tell me. Don't tell me. Mother.

1039
01:29:08,690 --> 01:29:10,450
What is it ?

1040
01:29:14,730 --> 01:29:18,350
Hooper, that's the USS Indianapolis.

1041
01:29:25,470 --> 01:29:27,440
- You were on the Indianapolis ?

1042
01:29:27,540 --> 01:29:28,800
- What happened ?

1043
01:29:30,840 --> 01:29:35,210
Japanese submarine slammed two torpedoes into her side.

1044
01:29:36,310 --> 01:29:40,320
Was comin' back from the island of Tinian Leyte.

1045
01:29:40,320 --> 01:29:44,690
Just delivered the bomb, the Hiroshima bomb.

1046
01:29:46,520 --> 01:29:49,120
Eleven hundred men went into the water.

1047
01:29:49,260 --> 01:29:52,160
Vessel went down in 1 2 minutes.

1048
01:29:53,700 --> 01:29:56,690
Didn't see the first shark for about half an hour.

1049
01:29:56,800 --> 01:30:01,430
Tiger, 1 3-footer. Know how you know that when you're in the water ?

1050
01:30:01,540 --> 01:30:04,470
You tell by lookin' from the dorsal to the tail.

1051
01:30:06,680 --> 01:30:08,740
What we didn't know

1052
01:30:08,850 --> 01:30:12,540
was our bomb mission had been so secret...

1053
01:30:12,650 --> 01:30:15,240
no distress signal had been sent.

1054
01:30:21,930 --> 01:30:25,230
They didn't even list us as overdue for a week.

1055
01:30:26,330 --> 01:30:30,200
Very first light, Chief, sharks come cruisin'.

1056
01:30:30,300 --> 01:30:33,030
We formed ourselves into tight groups.

1057
01:30:34,270 --> 01:30:40,000
Kinda like old squares in a battle, like you see on a calendar, like the Battle of Waterloo.

1058
01:30:40,080 --> 01:30:42,980
The idea was, shark comes to the nearest man,

1059
01:30:43,080 --> 01:30:45,810
that man starts poundin', hollerin', screamin'.

1060
01:30:45,950 --> 01:30:48,480
Sometimes the shark go away,

1061
01:30:49,590 --> 01:30:51,780
sometimes he wouldn't go away.

1062
01:30:51,890 --> 01:30:54,590
Sometimes that shark looks right into ya,

1063
01:30:54,730 --> 01:30:57,320
right into your eyes.

1064
01:30:57,460 --> 01:31:02,230
You know, a thing about a shark, he's got lifeless eyes.

1065
01:31:02,330 --> 01:31:05,030
Black eyes, like a doll's eyes.

1066
01:31:06,170 --> 01:31:09,870
When he comes at ya, doesn't seem to be livin',

1067
01:31:09,970 --> 01:31:11,600
until he bites ya and those black eyes roll over wide.

1068
01:31:11,710 --> 01:31:16,580
And then--

1069
01:31:16,580 --> 01:31:20,280
then you hear that terrible high-pitched screamin'.

1070
01:31:20,380 --> 01:31:22,650
The ocean turns red.

1071
01:31:22,750 --> 01:31:26,660
In spite of the pounding and hollering, they all come in.

1072
01:31:28,290 --> 01:31:30,190
They rip you to pieces.

1073
01:31:34,870 --> 01:31:37,430
You know, by the end of that first dawn,

1074
01:31:39,040 --> 01:31:40,940
lost a hundred men.

1075
01:31:42,240 --> 01:31:44,500
I don't know how many sharks, maybe a thousand.

1076
01:31:44,610 --> 01:31:46,940
I don't know how many men. They averaged six an hour.

1077
01:31:47,080 --> 01:31:49,910
On Thursday morning,

1078
01:31:50,010 --> 01:31:53,540
I bumped into a friend of mine, Robinson, from Cleveland,

1079
01:31:54,990 --> 01:31:58,150
baseball player, boatswain's mate.

1080
01:31:59,820 --> 01:32:02,310
I thought he was asleep.

1081
01:32:02,460 --> 01:32:05,430
Reached over to wake him up.

1082
01:32:05,530 --> 01:32:09,900
Bobbed up and down in the water like a top.

1083
01:32:10,000 --> 01:32:11,560
Upended.

1084
01:32:13,400 --> 01:32:18,310
Well, he'd been bitten in half below the waist.

1085
01:32:20,310 --> 01:32:23,610
Noon the fifth day, Mr. Hooper,

1086
01:32:23,710 --> 01:32:27,480
a Lockheed Ventura saw us. He swung in low and saw us.

1087
01:32:27,480 --> 01:32:30,250
Young pilot, a lot younger than Mr. Hooper.

1088
01:32:30,350 --> 01:32:33,190
He saw us and come in low. Three hours later,

1089
01:32:33,320 --> 01:32:36,820
a big fat PBY comes down and starts to pick us up.

1090
01:32:36,930 --> 01:32:40,390
That was the time I was most frightened,

1091
01:32:40,500 --> 01:32:42,400
waitin' for my turn.

1092
01:32:43,700 --> 01:32:46,640
I'll never put on a life jacket again.

1093
01:32:48,310 --> 01:32:51,240
Eleven hundred men went into the water.

1094
01:32:51,340 --> 01:32:53,240
31 6 men come out. The sharks took the rest.

1095
01:32:53,340 --> 01:32:59,280
June 29, 1 945.

1096
01:33:00,280 --> 01:33:01,510
Anyway,

1097
01:33:02,650 --> 01:33:04,710
we delivered the bomb.

1098
01:33:16,370 --> 01:33:18,460
What's that ?

1099
01:33:18,570 --> 01:33:20,430
It's a whale.

1100
01:33:21,570 --> 01:33:23,840
# Farewell and adieu #

1101
01:33:23,940 --> 01:33:27,040
# To you fair Spanish ladies #

1102
01:33:28,080 --> 01:33:30,310
# Farewell #

1103
01:33:30,410 --> 01:33:33,580
and adieu you ladies of Spain

1104
01:33:37,350 --> 01:33:41,310
# Show me the way to go home #

1105
01:33:42,860 --> 01:33:47,230
# I'm tired and I wanna go to bed #

1106
01:33:48,400 --> 01:33:50,870
# I had a little drink  #

1107
01:33:51,000 --> 01:33:53,440
about an hour ago

1108
01:33:53,540 --> 01:33:57,560
# And it's gone right to my head #

1109
01:33:58,680 --> 01:34:02,580
# Wherever I may roam #

1110
01:34:03,680 --> 01:34:07,710
# By land or sea or foam #

1111
01:34:07,920 --> 01:34:14,620
You will always hear me singin'this song [ Beeping ]

1112
01:34:14,760 --> 01:34:17,190
Show me the way to go home

1113
01:34:17,290 --> 01:34:22,230
# Boom, boom, boom Show me the way to go home #

1114
01:34:22,330 --> 01:34:25,320
# Boom, boom I'm tired and I wanna go to bed #

1115
01:34:25,440 --> 01:34:30,070
# I had a little drink about an hour ago # # And it went right to my head #

1116
01:34:30,970 --> 01:34:32,870
Wherever I may roam [ Banging ]

1117
01:34:32,980 --> 01:34:35,970
# On land or sea or foam #

1118
01:34:36,080 --> 01:34:38,740
# You can always hear me singing-- # [ Indistinct Noise ]

1119
01:34:42,250 --> 01:34:44,350
Start the engines.

1120
01:34:51,660 --> 01:34:55,860
[ Quint ] Fire her up ! Start the mill.

1121
01:34:56,830 --> 01:34:58,730
[ Hooper ] Busting shaft.

1122
01:35:03,270 --> 01:35:05,500
Chief, put out the fire, will ya ?

1123
01:35:15,320 --> 01:35:17,220
Pump her out. Done.

1124
01:35:25,660 --> 01:35:27,960
[ Quint ] Everybody on deck. [ Hooper ] He ate the light.

1125
01:35:28,070 --> 01:35:29,970
[ Brody ] Terrific. Excuse me.

1126
01:35:32,370 --> 01:35:37,030
[ Hooper ] Quint, what are you doing ? Don't waste your time.

1127
01:35:37,140 --> 01:35:39,940
[ Quint ] What's wrong with this shark ?

1128
01:35:40,040 --> 01:35:42,650
[ Quint ] Hooper, take the wheel.

1129
01:35:42,650 --> 01:35:44,880
Brody, forward deck. Watch for him.

1130
01:36:02,600 --> 01:36:04,190
You okay ?

1131
01:36:04,300 --> 01:36:07,100
Hey, Martin, you okay ?

1132
01:36:31,460 --> 01:36:35,360
[ Quint ] Hey, Chief, more left rudder. Pull your left hand down.

1133
01:36:35,470 --> 01:36:39,090
I can't. It'll only go about three inches.

1134
01:36:39,170 --> 01:36:40,760
[ Hooper ] Our injectors got scored from

1135
01:36:40,870 --> 01:36:43,930
the salt water in the fuel.

1136
01:36:44,040 --> 01:36:47,200
[ Quint ] The housing's bent. You can hear it.

1137
01:36:47,310 --> 01:36:49,340
Try the left rudder again, will ya ?

1138
01:36:49,450 --> 01:36:52,380
More left, good. Once again, now.

1139
01:36:53,480 --> 01:36:56,750
Quint, Quint, Quint ! There it is.

1140
01:36:56,850 --> 01:36:59,080
What do you say, Chief?

1141
01:36:59,190 --> 01:37:01,090
The barrel is up. It's right in the stern.

1142
01:37:06,060 --> 01:37:10,730
Think he's right under the keg. Grab the boat hook.

1143
01:37:20,880 --> 01:37:23,900
Quint, if we can get close enough,

1144
01:37:24,010 --> 01:37:26,350
I've got things on board that'll kill him.

1145
01:37:26,450 --> 01:37:28,850
Just want to goose him up. Come on.

1146
01:37:36,530 --> 01:37:38,990
Okay.

1147
01:37:41,300 --> 01:37:44,730
When he runs, drop that rope or you'll lose your hands.

1148
01:37:46,170 --> 01:37:48,900
I seen fingers torn out at the knuckles.

1149
01:37:49,010 --> 01:37:53,470
Whole sea's full of'em. Give it to me a minute.

1150
01:38:08,190 --> 01:38:11,090
[ Quint ] Haul in that line or it will foul us.

1151
01:38:11,190 --> 01:38:12,590
Start the engines.

1152
01:38:14,560 --> 01:38:18,760
- Where you goin' ? - I'm gonna make a phone call.

1153
01:38:22,670 --> 01:38:24,830
Hello ? Hello ?

1154
01:38:24,940 --> 01:38:28,310
Hello, Mayday ! Orca. Coast Guard ?

1155
01:38:28,410 --> 01:38:31,140
[ Brody ] Coast Guard, this is Orca. Do you read me ?

1156
01:38:31,250 --> 01:38:32,510
Coast Guard, this is Orca, do you--

1157
01:38:39,790 --> 01:38:41,550
Excuse me, Chief.

1158
01:38:41,690 --> 01:38:44,820
That's great ! That's just great !

1159
01:38:44,960 --> 01:38:46,990
Now where the hell are we, huh ?

1160
01:38:48,300 --> 01:38:50,930
You're certifiable, Quint, do you know that ?

1161
01:38:51,030 --> 01:38:53,470
You're certifiable ! Yeah, yeah, yeah.

1162
01:38:55,170 --> 01:38:57,040
[ Hooper ] Boys. Oh, boys.

1163
01:38:57,140 --> 01:38:59,510
I think he's come back for his noon feeding.

1164
01:39:01,210 --> 01:39:02,610
Hook me up another barrel !

1165
01:39:32,210 --> 01:39:35,010
Take her around after him !

1166
01:39:50,590 --> 01:39:54,900
[ Quint ] Full throttle! Get me right up alongside him.

1167
01:39:54,900 --> 01:39:59,230
[ Hooper ] I can't! It's not gonna take it!

1168
01:40:15,020 --> 01:40:18,110
Five degrees port.

1169
01:40:24,730 --> 01:40:27,160
All right, hold your course.

1170
01:40:32,900 --> 01:40:34,800
Five degrees port now.

1171
01:40:38,410 --> 01:40:39,970
Hold your course.

1172
01:40:41,080 --> 01:40:43,640
Fast fish. [ Quint ] Watch my hand.

1173
01:40:44,750 --> 01:40:49,350
Be sure you watch my hand now. Follow me. Follow me.

1174
01:40:49,420 --> 01:40:52,580
All right, watch now. Starboard, starboard!

1175
01:40:53,720 --> 01:40:55,710
Run him down, Hooper.

1176
01:40:57,260 --> 01:40:58,590
Run him down ! Run him down !

1177
01:41:02,700 --> 01:41:03,860
Hard aport !

1178
01:41:07,800 --> 01:41:11,870
[ Quint ] Watch him ! Starboard! Starboard!

1179
01:41:33,030 --> 01:41:36,900
[ Brody ] I can't believe it! Two barrels and he's going down again.

1180
01:41:42,870 --> 01:41:44,700
He's incredible.

1181
01:41:50,850 --> 01:41:52,750
They're up again ! Now what ?

1182
01:42:02,130 --> 01:42:04,180
Why don't we lead the shark to shore instead

1183
01:42:04,330 --> 01:42:06,350
of him leading us to sea ?

1184
01:42:10,630 --> 01:42:12,630
Grab a couple of poles, okay ?

1185
01:42:14,670 --> 01:42:16,870
Hang on now, we're goin' around.

1186
01:42:16,970 --> 01:42:19,810
[ Quint ] Into starboard, easy.

1187
01:42:21,010 --> 01:42:26,010
I'm gonna back her up now. Watch those barrels, boys. Watch them !

1188
01:42:29,490 --> 01:42:31,220
All right, gentlemen, snag 'em.

1189
01:42:37,630 --> 01:42:39,360
Now then, tie them to the stern cleats.

1190
01:42:42,670 --> 01:42:45,500
Brody, bring your end around the cleat!

1191
01:42:46,440 --> 01:42:47,930
That's right. It'll lock itself off.

1192
01:42:48,040 --> 01:42:51,030
Give him room, Brody!

1193
01:42:51,140 --> 01:42:54,700
Aaah ! Stay clear of the line!

1194
01:43:01,320 --> 01:43:02,810
Watch it. Stand clear.

1195
01:43:13,160 --> 01:43:15,690
Stand away from those stern cleats !

1196
01:43:28,710 --> 01:43:30,980
Back home we got a taxidermy man.

1197
01:43:31,080 --> 01:43:34,710
He gonna have a heart attack when he see what I brung.

1198
01:43:41,060 --> 01:43:43,620
Throttle back ! You're losing your cleats !

1199
01:43:44,490 --> 01:43:49,260
[ Hooper ] Look at that mother. This one too. They're both going.

1200
01:43:49,370 --> 01:43:51,660
He's eating his way right through that line.

1201
01:43:51,770 --> 01:43:54,000
Yeah, he's working his way right up to us. Quint !

1202
01:43:54,100 --> 01:43:56,070
[ Hooper ] Come on, Quint!

1203
01:43:56,810 --> 01:43:57,770
Hurry! Quint!

1204
01:43:58,840 --> 01:44:00,330
Out of my way.

1205
01:44:05,280 --> 01:44:06,210
[ Quint ] Watch it!

1206
01:44:10,420 --> 01:44:12,910
Untie us ! He'll pull out the transom !

1207
01:44:16,560 --> 01:44:18,750
[ Quint ] Make it fast! We'll get another line in him.

1208
01:44:18,900 --> 01:44:20,490
I can't ! He's trying to run !

1209
01:44:22,000 --> 01:44:23,970
[ Quint ] He's gonna give us a ride!

1210
01:44:24,070 --> 01:44:26,540
[ Quint ] Pull, you son of a bitch.

1211
01:44:26,640 --> 01:44:28,600
Hope your back breaks ! Go on !

1212
01:44:28,710 --> 01:44:31,140
Pull your bloody heart out !

1213
01:44:31,240 --> 01:44:32,710
Tie him off ! Do it. Tie him off !

1214
01:44:37,610 --> 01:44:40,140
It's impossible ! It's impossible !

1215
01:44:41,520 --> 01:44:44,420
The line is too tight. He's towing us !

1216
01:44:44,520 --> 01:44:47,290
Cut him loose or he'll pull the transom off !

1217
01:44:47,420 --> 01:44:50,860
[ Hooper ] We're breaking up ! Cut it, man. It's coming off !

1218
01:44:50,860 --> 01:44:54,590
[ Hooper ] The ax! Get the ax!

1219
01:44:54,730 --> 01:44:56,200
We're breaking up ! We're breaking up !

1220
01:44:57,930 --> 01:45:00,460
Cut it ! Cut it ! Watch your hands!

1221
01:45:00,570 --> 01:45:03,630
Come on ! Hold it ! [ Hooper ] Cut it! I can't hold it!

1222
01:45:03,740 --> 01:45:06,000
Cut it! Cut it!

1223
01:45:24,760 --> 01:45:27,160
Can't stay down with three barrels on him.

1224
01:45:27,260 --> 01:45:29,700
Not with three barrels, he can't.

1225
01:45:29,800 --> 01:45:31,700
What about us ? Hooper,

1226
01:45:31,800 --> 01:45:35,600
get the pump out of the locker, will you ?

1227
01:45:35,710 --> 01:45:36,870
We're gonna sink, aren't we ?

1228
01:45:36,970 --> 01:45:39,070
Hooper, keep an eye on the barrels.

1229
01:45:39,180 --> 01:45:40,700
Pump it out, Chief.

1230
01:45:47,220 --> 01:45:48,840
Trying to go under !

1231
01:45:48,950 --> 01:45:51,890
He can't with three barrels on him.

1232
01:46:27,220 --> 01:46:29,490
You ever have one do this before ?

1233
01:46:31,630 --> 01:46:32,600
Hell, no.

1234
01:46:44,340 --> 01:46:46,240
[ Banging ] [ Quint ] Hold fast!

1235
01:47:04,230 --> 01:47:06,220
[ Hooper ] He's chasing us. I don't believe it.

1236
01:47:11,870 --> 01:47:14,340
I'm gonna draw him into the shallows.

1237
01:47:14,440 --> 01:47:17,770
Draw him into shallow water, draw him in and drown him.

1238
01:47:19,080 --> 01:47:21,410
We're headin' in, Brody. Thank Christ.

1239
01:47:29,250 --> 01:47:31,650
Have you ever had a great white do this ? No !

1240
01:47:37,990 --> 01:47:39,990
How far do we have to go ?

1241
01:47:42,700 --> 01:47:44,720
Quint, don't put that much pressure on them.

1242
01:47:55,250 --> 01:47:58,510
Quint, goddamn it ! Shut up ! Get back there !

1243
01:47:58,620 --> 01:48:00,850
I'll break the engine-- It's gonna tear up--

1244
01:48:03,690 --> 01:48:04,850
Hold on, Martin.

1245
01:48:19,770 --> 01:48:22,860
# Farewell and adieu #

1246
01:48:22,970 --> 01:48:25,670
# You fair Spanish ladies #

1247
01:48:27,410 --> 01:48:29,380
# Farewell and adieu #

1248
01:48:29,480 --> 01:48:32,450
You ladies of Spain

1249
01:48:33,980 --> 01:48:38,960
For we received orders For to sail back to Boston

1250
01:48:38,960 --> 01:48:41,390
You idiot, you burned out the bearings.

1251
01:48:43,660 --> 01:48:48,030
[ Brody ] All right, stop the boat. Stop the boat ! Stop it !

1252
01:50:04,410 --> 01:50:05,810
Hooper !

1253
01:50:06,910 --> 01:50:08,380
Chief.

1254
01:50:24,990 --> 01:50:28,900
Hooper, what exactly can you do with these things of yours ?

1255
01:50:33,570 --> 01:50:37,940
Well, I think I can pump 20 ccs of strychnine nitrate into him,

1256
01:50:38,010 --> 01:50:40,000
if I can get close enough.

1257
01:50:43,280 --> 01:50:45,410
Can you get this little needle through his skin ?

1258
01:50:47,750 --> 01:50:49,650
No, I can't do that.

1259
01:50:51,090 --> 01:50:54,280
But if I can get him close enough to this cage, I could get him in the mouth.

1260
01:50:54,420 --> 01:50:57,550
That shark will rip that cage -- You got any better suggestions ?

1261
01:51:23,650 --> 01:51:25,250
Easy, easy.

1262
01:51:25,350 --> 01:51:28,020
All right, up she goes.

1263
01:51:30,030 --> 01:51:32,260
Ease her up.

1264
01:52:23,380 --> 01:52:25,110
I ain't got no spit.

1265
01:52:39,260 --> 01:52:42,230
Try and keep him off me until I'm lower.

1266
01:52:44,570 --> 01:52:47,260
Okay, okay, I'm ready.

1267
01:55:43,180 --> 01:55:45,810
Bring him up, goddamn it !

1268
01:55:45,920 --> 01:55:47,410
Bring him up now !

1269
01:55:52,690 --> 01:55:54,160
Pull it up ! Pull it !

1270
01:56:01,030 --> 01:56:04,360
Bring him up. What are you waiting for?

1271
01:56:04,470 --> 01:56:06,530
Come on, Quint, bring him in.

1272
01:56:10,370 --> 01:56:11,340
It's giving way !

1273
01:56:23,790 --> 01:56:25,340
Rig something. Rig something!

1274
01:56:29,190 --> 01:56:29,920
Got it ? All right.

1275
01:56:30,360 --> 01:56:32,330
Got it ? All right.

1276
01:56:32,600 --> 01:56:36,270
It's coming. Slower.

1277
01:56:36,270 --> 01:56:38,460
Slower!

1278
01:59:53,030 --> 01:59:59,670
Come on, show me the tank. Blow up !

1279
02:00:13,480 --> 02:00:14,850
Blow up !

1280
02:00:18,550 --> 02:00:20,020
Smile, you son-of-a-bitch !

1281
02:01:49,680 --> 02:01:54,210
Quint ? No.

1282
02:02:02,190 --> 02:02:04,160
Can we get in on those ?

1283
02:02:09,030 --> 02:02:11,900
Hey, what day is this ?

1284
02:02:14,540 --> 02:02:17,200
It's Wednesday -- it's Tuesday, I think.

1285
02:02:18,610 --> 02:02:20,580
I think the tide's with us.

1286
02:02:21,680 --> 02:02:23,140
Keep kickin'.

1287
02:02:26,380 --> 02:02:28,680
I used to hate the water.

1288
02:02:30,590 --> 02:02:32,880
I can't imagine why.

